WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.655
A Hive shares market information and a ledger between local
Minecraft instances. Each account keeps its

00:00:10.655 --> 00:00:18.000
settings, orders, limits and recovery state. Headless mode is
optional.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:29.368
Open Accounts, Hive setup. Review locally detected accounts. In
the browser panel, Hive and commands can add

00:00:29.368 --> 00:00:36.000
a fresh detected bot to an existing Hive without a game window.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:45.801
For the disconnected wizard, open Multiplayer, GoNuts hive.
Share this hive on the existing account; use

00:00:45.801 --> 00:00:54.000
Link accounts and Review connection on the new instance. Keep
the original data folder.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:04.517
Choose Join existing hive for a fresh account. Existing
histories use the separate supported combination

00:01:04.517 --> 00:01:12.000
flow. Never delete order records or a shared database to bypass
a refusal.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:23.435
After a new-account join confirms, restart only that new
instance normally. Joining does not enable trading.

00:01:23.435 --> 00:01:30.000
The original settings and recovery gates remain authoritative.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:39.000
Use the account selector on Money and Orders. One account shows
only that account. All accounts combines the

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:47.333
Hive. Unfilled order funds and delivered goods awaiting
collection stay separate from auction asking

00:01:47.333 --> 00:01:48.000
revenue.
